cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below (and the HAZBRA data paper once published)."
title: "HAZBRA: processing code of a climate hazard dataset for Brazil"
type: software
version: 0.1.1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Luisgcattelan/HAZBRA"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24319623
abstract: >-
  Code that computes the HAZBRA climate-hazard indicators for Brazil (16 rainfall, drought, heat and
  compound indicators) from CHIRPS, MERGE and BR-DWGD observations and the 19-model CLIMBRA CMIP6
  ensemble at global warming levels of 1.5, 2 and 3 °C, with GEV return levels, return-period shifts,
  ensemble statistics, delta-change projections and municipal aggregation.
keywords: [climate hazards, extremes, Brazil, CMIP6, CLIMBRA, global warming levels, return periods, GEV]
